.TH MORPH 1 "2025" "morph 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
morph \- universal data format converter with mapping language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B morph
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIINPUT\fR] [\fIOUTPUT\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B morph
is a universal CLI data format converter with a mapping language.
It supports converting between JSON, YAML, TOML, CSV, XML, MessagePack,
and JSON Lines formats.
.PP
The mapping language provides operations like rename, select, drop, set,
cast, where, each, when, flatten, nest, sort, and default. It includes
30+ built-in functions for string, math, collection, and type operations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " " \fIFILE\fR
Input file (reads from stdin if not specified)
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Output file (writes to stdout if not specified)
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-from " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Input format (auto-detected from file extension if not specified)
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-to " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format (auto-detected from file extension if not specified)
.TP
.BR \-\-pretty
Pretty-print output (default for TTY)
.TP
.BR \-\-compact
Compact output (default for pipes)
.TP
.BR \-\-indent " " \fIN\fR
Indentation width in spaces
.TP
.BR \-\-formats
List supported formats and exit
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mapping " " \fIFILE\fR
Apply a mapping file (.morph)
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-expr " " \fIEXPRESSION\fR
Inline mapping expression (can be repeated)
.TP
.BR \-\-dry\-run
Parse and validate the mapping without executing
.TP
.BR \-\-csv\-delimiter " " \fICHAR\fR
CSV field delimiter character (default: comma)
.TP
.BR \-\-csv\-no\-header
Input CSV has no header row
.TP
.BR \-\-csv\-header " " \fINAMES\fR
Override CSV headers (comma-separated field names)
.TP
.BR \-\-xml\-root " " \fINAME\fR
Root element name for XML output (default: "root")
.TP
.BR \-\-xml\-attr\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Attribute prefix for XML (default: "@")
.TP
.BR \-\-yaml\-multi\-doc
Treat YAML input as multi-document (return array of documents)
.TP
.BR \-\-yaml\-doc\-marker
Include document start marker (---) in YAML output
.TP
.BR \-\-csv\-always\-quote
Always quote CSV fields
.TP
.BR \-\-csv\-quote\-style " " \fISTYLE\fR
CSV quote style: always, never, necessary, non_numeric (default: necessary)
.TP
.BR \-\-csv\-null\-string " " \fISTRING\fR
String to use for null values in CSV (default: empty)
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
.TS
tab(|) nospaces;
l l.
Format|Extensions
_
JSON|json
JSONL|jsonl, ndjson
YAML|yaml, yml
TOML|toml
CSV|csv
XML|xml
MessagePack|msgpack, mp
.TE
.SH MAPPING LANGUAGE
The mapping language allows transforming data during conversion.
.SS Operations
.TS
tab(|) nospaces;
l l.
Operation|Description
_
rename|Rename fields
select|Select specific fields
drop|Drop specific fields
set|Set field values
cast|Cast values to types
where|Filter records
each|Apply expression to each element
when|Conditional operations
flatten|Flatten nested structures
nest|Nest fields into sub-objects
sort|Sort arrays
default|Set default values
.TE
.SS Built-in Functions
String functions: upper, lower, trim, replace, split, join, slice, len, contains, starts_with, ends_with
.PP
Math functions: abs, floor, ceil, round, sqrt, pow, min, max, sum, avg
.PP
Collection functions: keys, values, entries, pick, omit, merge, reverse, unique, group_by
.PP
Type functions: type, is_null, is_bool, is_num, is_str, is_arr, is_obj
.PP
Other functions: now, uuid, random, hash, encode, decode, format, parse
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert JSON to YAML:
.PP
.nf
.RS
morph input.json output.yaml
.RE
.fi
.PP
Convert CSV to JSON with pretty printing:
.PP
.nf
.RS
morph data.csv --to json --pretty
.RE
.fi
.PP
Apply a mapping file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
morph input.json output.yaml -m transform.morph
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inline mapping to rename fields:
.PP
.nf
.RS
morph input.json output.json -e 'rename(old_name: new_name)'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Filter and select:
.PP
.nf
.RS
morph data.json --to yaml -e 'where(age > 18)' -e 'select(name, email)'
.RE
.fi
.PP
Read from stdin, write to stdout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
cat data.json | morph --from json --to yaml --pretty
.RE
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR NO_COLOR
Set to any value to disable colored output
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments
.TP
.B 3
Input/output error
.TP
.B 4
Parse error
.TP
.B 5
Mapping error
.TP
.B 6
Format error
.TP
.B 7
Conversion error
.TP
.B 8
Validation error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/morph/
User configuration directory
.TP
.I *.morph
Mapping files
